ascii 1:1 -> 0:0
ascii 1:5 -> 0:4
ascii 2:1 -> 1:0
2-byte at 1:1 -> 0:0
2-byte at 1:12 (before e) -> 0:11
2-byte at 1:13 (on e) -> 0:12
2-byte at 1:14 (2nd byte of e) -> 0:13
2-byte at 1:16 (the semicolon) -> 0:14
3-byte at 1:11 (before) -> 0:10
3-byte at 1:14 (after) -> 0:11
4-byte at 1:11 (before) -> 0:11
4-byte at 1:15 (on it) -> 0:12
4-byte at 1:18 (after) -> 0:13
mixed 1:1 -> 0:0
mixed 1:5 (on e-acute) -> 0:4
mixed 1:15 -> 0:13
src_line(0) = 1  src_line(9) = 10  src_line(-1) = 1
back ascii 0:4 -> col 5
back 2byte 0:12 -> col 13
back 4byte 0:14 -> col 16
bytes 8  chars 5
round trip at every character start: 1
every character index reachable: 1
line 99 -> 98:0
col 999 -> 0:10
